<h1>VoiceTel Phone for Linux.</h1>
<p class="lede">Download, install, and troubleshoot the Linux app: AppImage, .deb, .rpm, Snap, or Flatpak, on x86-64 and arm64. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is listed alongside.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Sign up</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
</p>

<section id="download" class="section-block">
	<h2>1. Download</h2>
	<p>Pick the package that matches your distro and CPU: <strong>x86-64 / amd64</strong> for Intel and AMD, <strong>arm64</strong> for 64-bit ARM such as Raspberry Pi 4/5. If you're unsure, use the <strong>AppImage</strong>.</p>
	{% include "partials/phone-desktop-downloads.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="verify" class="section-block">
	<h2>2. Verify checksum (optional)</h2>
	<p>Validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums.</p>
	<ol>
		<li>Open your terminal.</li>
		<li>Run: <code>sha256sum VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.AppImage</code> (or whichever file you downloaded).</li>
		<li>Compare the output with the value listed above.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="install" class="section-block">
	<h2>3. Install</h2>
	<p>Commands below use the VoiceTel Phone x86-64 file names; substitute the file you downloaded (for example <code>-arm64</code> or <code>VoiceML-</code>).</p>
	<h3>AppImage</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Run <code>chmod +x VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.AppImage</code>, or right-click the file &rarr; <em>Properties</em> &rarr; <em>Permissions</em> and enable <em>Allow executing file as program</em>.</li>
		<li>Double-click to launch (optional: move to <code>~/Applications</code>).</li>
	</ol>
	<h3>Debian / Ubuntu</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Open Terminal in the download directory.</li>
		<li>Run <code>sudo apt install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.deb</code>.</li>
	</ol>
	<h3>Fedora / RHEL / openSUSE</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Open Terminal in the download directory.</li>
		<li>Run <code>sudo dnf install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.rpm</code>.</li>
	</ol>
	<h3>Snap</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Run <code>sudo snap install --dangerous ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.snap</code>.</li>
	</ol>
	<h3>Flatpak</h3>
	<ol>
		<li>Run <code>flatpak install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.flatpak</code>.</li>
	</ol>
	<p><strong>Upgrading?</strong> Fully quit the running app from the system tray (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version.</p>
</section>

<section id="firstlaunch" class="section-block">
	<h2>4. First launch</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Start <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML</strong>) from your app launcher.</li>
		<li>Allow microphone access if your desktop environment prompts for it.</li>
		<li>Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section-block faq-block">
	<h2>FAQ</h2>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>How do I uninstall?</summary>
		<p><strong>AppImage:</strong> delete the file. <strong>Debian / Ubuntu:</strong> <code>sudo apt remove voicetel-phone</code>. <strong>Fedora / Red Hat:</strong> <code>sudo rpm -e voicetel-phone</code>.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>No audio device or PipeWire issues</summary>
		<p>Verify PulseAudio or PipeWire is running and select the correct input/output device in your system sound settings.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Wayland screen sharing</summary>
		<p>Install <code>xdg-desktop-portal</code> and your desktop-environment-specific portal (e.g. <code>xdg-desktop-portal-gnome</code> or <code>-kde</code>).</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Pre-seed configuration</summary>
		<p>User: <code>~/.config/VoiceTelPhone/voicetel.json</code> &middot; System-wide: <code>/etc/VoiceTelPhone/voicetel.json</code>.</p>
	</details>
</section>

